the north stream 2 gas pipeline has  proven a contentious topic in u.s  european relations but washington this  week said it was dropping its opposition  to the project  after reaching a deal with berlin the  pipeline's supposed to  double the volume of gas delivered to  germany via the baltic sea but critics  say it will give russia  too much scope to control energy  supplies to ukraine  or other european nations dw's moscow  bureau chief talked to  former russian president dmitry medvedev  about it  the kremlin is one of the biggest  stakeholders in the german-american deal  former russian president dmitry medvedev  told dw  that the agreement would pave the way  for the completion of nordstream 2.  positive words even though the agreement  pledges action if russia uses the  pipeline as a weapon  to disrupt gas flows through ukraine  even though we don't like a few  formulations and there are a couple of  clauses on sanctions  it's still better than destroying a  nearly finished project that is so  important for europe  and you're not afraid of a couple of  clauses sanctions as you say if russia  were to stop transporting gas through  ukraine  if someone imposes sanctions we would  survive  but i think something else is happening  right now  we're seeing european and american  politicians performing a ritual dance  to recognize the fact that the nordstrom  2 project has succeeded  rejects the criticism from nordstrom 2  opponents  that the pipeline will leave germany too  dependent on russia  for its energy needs  you can never be too dependent when it  comes to trade  trade is always mutual if germany is  dependent on russian gas supplies  then russia is dependent on the market  prices  and certain delivery volumes being  approved  medvedev is convinced that the nordstrom  2 project is not political but rather  commercial  he feels that the u.s created  difficulties on the path to completion  out of its own self-interest  at a certain point our interests clashed  with those of the united states  washington realized it's much more  profitable to supply europe with its own  liquid gas  and earn money doing it the americans  applied pressure  and noise stream 2 became problematic  these problems are down to u.s economic  interests  and its attempts to profit from the  european market  moscow says it regrets that germany and  the us agreed their deal without  russia's participation  kremlin speaker dimitri piskov compared  it to holding a wedding without the  groom  and rejected the accusation that russia  had ever used the supply of natural gas  as a political instrument  you
 

